ift. We need to provide evidence for A and compare. Let's examine A's facts: anticipates dangerous situations, sees complex connections, excellent spatial vision, very good leadership qualities, unfriendly, eats unhealthily, sometimes not good at taking criticism, not organized, show\u2011off, not open to new ideas. Strengths: anticipates danger (decision quality), sees complex connections (technical competence), spatial vision (technical), leadership (crew cooperation). Weaknesses: unfriendly (crew cooperation), eats unhealthily (reliability/health), not good at taking criticism (feedback), not organized (reliability), show\u2011off, not open to new ideas (adaptability). So A has strong technical and leadership but poor cooperation and reliability concerns. Compared to C: C has reliability, decision quality, attention, crew atmosphere, calm, but communication difficulty and egocentric, not willing to further education. Which is better? Both have communication issues. A's unfriendly may be more severe. C's egocentric maybe similar. A's health concerns (eating unhealthily) could affect long-haul. So likely C remains stronger.\n\nThus as Agent 3, we can agree with Agent 2 that C is the leading candidate, but we need to bring up A for completeness, and argue that A's weaknesses (unfriendly, health, lack of organization) make him less suitable than C. So we keep recommendation for C, but note that we have now covered A and C, and we can move toward convergence.\n\nThus public message: I agree with Agent 2 that C is strongest, and I will add that Candidate A, while showing strong technical anticipation and leadership, has significant reliability and crew cooperation concerns (unfriendly, not organized, health), making him less suitable than C. Therefore I maintain recommendation for C and suggest we can now move toward final decision, pending any remaining questions.\n\nProvide metadata JSON with vote Candidate C.\n\nProceed."}
